  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "There are two blue and three red balls placed in a bag. One ball is selected. If the ball is red, then it is returned to the bag. Otherwise it is discarded. A second ball is then drawn from the bag. Find the probability that:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "both balls have the same colour",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{23}{50}$",
          "worked": "Let $R$ denote red and $B$ denote blue. After a red draw the bag is unchanged; after a blue draw only one blue ball remains among four balls.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(RR)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac35\\\\P(RR)&=\\frac9{25}\\\\P(BB)&=\\frac25\\times\\frac14\\\\P(BB)&=\\frac1{10}\\\\P(\\text{same colour})&=\\frac9{25}+\\frac1{10}\\\\P(\\text{same colour})&=\\frac{23}{50}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "both balls are red given that both balls have the same colour.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{18}{23}$",
          "worked": "The same-colour outcomes are $RR$ and $BB$. Using part (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}P(RR\\mid\\text{same colour})&=\\frac{P(RR)}{P(\\text{same colour})}\\\\P(RR\\mid\\text{same colour})&=\\frac{9/25}{23/50}\\\\P(RR\\mid\\text{same colour})&=\\frac{18}{23}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
  },
